invariant: INV-36
file: Makefile
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: the Makefile's host test stops asking for NEON or SSE2, so a
  compiler for an arm64 core without NEON or an x86-64 core without SSE2
  gives a TRUST=webpki object -DCH_CPU_RUNTIME, which cpu_cfg.h then
  refuses at compile time. test/host-builds.sh requires the Makefile to
  pass no define under a compiler for either target.

--- old
  printf '%s\n' "$$macros" | grep -qwE '__ARM_NEON|__SSE2__' && \
--- new
